NV_PK(30,{"its name comes from the jingmei area which joined muzha to form wenshan district in 1990":"","before 1700 the basin belonged to the basay people who spoke ketagalan in the 1700s han settlers arrived and built bangka by the river after a clan feud in 1853 the tongan people moved north and built dadaocheng which grew rich on tea when tamsui opened as a treaty port in 1860 in 1884 the qing finished a walled city with five gates taipei's third town":"","in 1895 japanese rule began and taipei became the colonial capital the city walls came down and wide tree lined boulevards went in new buildings of brick and stone appeared the red house the governor general's office and the museum in the park in 1920 the three old towns were joined into taipei city":""});